   $q$How do the very short sentences 5 and 6 affect the pacing?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They slow the narrative down so the reader can admire the scenery.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"They signal a shift from the narrator's point of view to Ms. Abiodun's.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-pov-shift"},{"text":"Their abrupt stop mirrors the jammed rope and creates a jolt of alarm.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They summarize several hours of rehearsal in just a few words.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pacing-speed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Their abrupt stop mirrors the jammed rope and creates a jolt of alarm.$q$, $q$"I pulled the rope. Nothing moved." stops the reader short just as the rope stops, so the form matches the event. The sentences cover a single second, not hours of rehearsal.$q$, 'draft', 'b6d6c2f9-3e24-5625-927f-10feea480caf')
