   $q$Which revision of sentence 10 best uses dialogue to develop Dr. Okonjo while keeping the information?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Dr. Okonjo leaned over the wood. \"Narrow rings usually mean a dry stretch. What was this tree living through?\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Hello,\" Dr. Okonjo said, and then told us that narrow rings mean a long dry period.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-off-point"},{"text":"Narrow rings often mean a long dry period, when a tree can barely grow at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-dialogue"},{"text":"Dr. Okonjo said something to us about how narrow rings might be important.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-information"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Dr. Okonjo leaned over the wood. "Narrow rings usually mean a dry stretch. What was this tree living through?"$q$, $q$The correct choice keeps the fact about dry periods and uses a question to show Dr. Okonjo as a teacher who prompts thinking. The "Hello" choice adds dialogue, but the spoken words do nothing for the story.$q$, 'draft', '08e5fce8-2851-59c4-becd-843df11d21c9')
